# Scorix design rules (Cursor)

Read `.interface-design/system.md` before visual changes.

## Stack

Vanilla hash-SPA. **No** React, Tailwind, bundler migration in visual tasks.

## Tokens (mandatory)

- Spacing: only `--space-1` (4px) through `--space-6` (32px)
- Colors: CSS variables from system.md — never hardcoded hex except in `:root` theme defs
- Fonts: `--display` (Syne) headings; `--font` (Manrope) UI

## Layout

- Prefer `display: flex` or `grid` with `gap: var(--space-N)` — not margin stacks
- One panel depth per block (`--surface`); nested `--surface-2` without shadow
- Flex for 1D rows; Grid for readiness strip, tables, admin density

## Components

- Import/reuse existing classes — don't duplicate button/panel styles
- Primary CTA: one per zone, `--accent`
- Touch targets ≥ 44×44px
- Tables: `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`

## Accessibility

- Semantic `button`, `label`+`input`, visible `:focus-visible`
- `aria-label` on icon-only controls
- Status readable without color alone

## Forbidden

- Purple AI glow, neon shadows, cream/terracotta palette
- Card-in-card, decorative cards, stat pill clusters
- Arbitrary px (10, 14, 20…) outside token scale
- Rewriting UI copy — strings from handoff/ux-write-design only

## Motion

- Transition `transform`, `opacity` — not `width`/`height`
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`

## SEO note

Public landing HTML: unique title/description per page. Authenticated `#/` routes: not for indexing.
